Documentation page for configuration files : https://docs.splunk.com/Documentation/Splunk/9.4.0/Admin/Configurationfilestructureandsyntax

Configuration block MUST start with a stanza [].



Rules :
files can start with empty or commented lines
Stanza (or section) stuff :
[FAIL]  configuration before stanza declaration !
[WARN]  empty stanza block
[FAIL]  pattern of section pattern [example:<target_list>]. Can be 1 or 2 : between exampel and target_list
[FAIL]  in [example:<target_list>], example is not [a-zA-Z0-9-_]
[FAIL]  in [example:<target_list>], target_list is not [a-zA-Z0-9-_*?+/]+
[FAIL]  any character before '['
[FAIL]  only accept space and comments after ']'

Config itself :
[FAIL]  not in format "[a-zA-Z0-9-_]+ {0,1}="
[WARN]  a variable is defined multiple times in the same perimeter


Examples of configuration files found in the documentation :
"""
$SPLUNK_HOME/etc/system/local/props.conf
```
[source::/opt/Locke/Logs/error*]
sourcetype = fatal-error
```

$SPLUNK_HOME/etc/apps/t2rss/local/props.conf
```
